<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" class="scroll-smooth">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Section 7: Managing Content Automatically | Astro Rebuild Plan</title>
    <script src="https://cdn.tailwindcss.com"></script>
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
    <style>
        body { font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; background-color: #FFFFFF; color: #000000; }
        .dark body { background-color: #000000; color: #FFFFFF; }
        .prose { color: inherit; max-width: 80ch; }
        .prose h1, .prose h2, .prose h3, .prose h4, .prose strong { color: inherit; }
        .prose p, .prose li { color: inherit; opacity: 0.9; @apply text-lg leading-relaxed; }
        .prose a { color: #2563EB; } .dark .prose a { color: #60A5FA; }
        .prose code:not(.code-block code) { @apply rounded-md px-1.5 py-1 text-base; background-color: #F3F4F6; color: #111827; } .dark .prose code:not(.code-block code) { background-color: #1F2937; color: #F9FAFB; }
        .code-block { background-color: #1F2937; color: #F9FAFB; @apply rounded-lg my-2 p-4 text-sm; }
        .header-text { color: #000000; } .dark .header-text { color: #FFFFFF; }
        .subheader-text { color: #4A5568; } .dark .subheader-text { color: #A0AEC0; }
        .accent-text { color: #2563EB; } .dark .accent-text { color: #60A5FA; }
        .footer { border-top: 1px solid #E2E8F0; } .dark .footer { border-top: 1px solid #374151; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="container mx-auto px-4 py-10 sm:py-16">
        <header class="mb-12">
            <a href="#" class="inline-flex items-center accent-text hover:underline mb-6 font-semibold">
                <svg class="w-5 h-5 mr-2" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M10 19l-7-7m0 0l7-7m-7 7h18"></path></svg>
                Back to Main Index
            </a>
            <p class="text-sm font-semibold accent-text tracking-wider uppercase">Section 7</p>
            <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold header-text leading-tight mt-1">Managing Content with Collections</h1>
            <h2 class="text-xl subheader-text mt-3">The Automated Way to Handle Projects & Blogs</h2>
        </header>
        <main class="prose mx-auto">
            <article>
                <p>Manually creating an `.astro` file for every project or blog post is not scalable. Astro's **Content Collections** are the solution. They provide an automated, type-safe way to manage and generate pages from local content files like Markdown.</p>
                
                <h3>Step 1: Create a Content Collection</h3>
                <p>All collections live inside a special `src/content/` directory.</p>
                <ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-2">
                    <li>Create a new folder named `content` inside your `src/` folder.</li>
                    <li>Inside `src/content/`, create a folder for each collection. Let's make one for `projects`. Your structure will be `src/content/projects/`.</li>
                </ol>

                <h3>Step 2: Define a Schema</h3>
                <p>A schema ensures all your projects have consistent frontmatter (the data at the top of a Markdown file). This prevents errors and makes your code predictable.</p>
                 <ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-2">
                    <li>In the `src/content/` folder, create a new file named `config.ts`.</li>
                    <li>Add the following code to define the "contract" for your projects. We'll require a title, a description, and a publication date for every project.</li>
                </ol>
                 <div class="code-block">
<pre><code>// src/content/config.ts
import { defineCollection, z } from 'astro:content';

const projectsCollection = defineCollection({
  // Type-check your frontmatter.
  // See https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/content-collections/#defining-a-collection-schema
  schema: z.object({
    title: z.string(),
    description: z.string(),
    pubDate: z.date(),
  }),
});

export const collections = {
  'projects': projectsCollection,
};
</code></pre>
                </div>

                <h3>Step 3: Add Content</h3>
                <p>Now, you can create your first project as a Markdown file.</p>
                <ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-2">
                   <li>Create a new file inside your projects collection: `src/content/projects/astro-rebuild-guide.md`.</li>
                   <li>Add the frontmatter that matches the schema, along with your content.</li>
                </ol>
                <div class="code-block">
<pre><code>---
title: "The Astro Website Rebuild Guide"
description: "A living document charting the progress of rebuilding my Astro site from scratch."
pubDate: 2025-06-22
---

This is the content of my first project. I can write anything I want here in Markdown.

- A list item
- Another list item
</code></pre>
                </div>


                <h3>Step 4: Generate Pages Automatically with a Dynamic Route</h3>
                <p>Instead of creating a new `.astro` page for every project, you create **one** dynamic template.</p>
                <ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-2">
                    <li>Create a new file at `src/pages/projects/[...slug].astro`. The square brackets and ellipses are special syntax that tells Astro this is a dynamic route.</li>
                    <li>Add the code below. This code fetches all projects, generates a static page for each one, and renders its content.</li>
                </ol>
                <div class="code-block">
<pre><code>---
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

// This function runs at build time to generate all the project pages
export async function getStaticPaths() {
  const projects = await getCollection('projects');
  return projects.map(project => ({
    params: { slug: project.slug },
    props: { project },
  }));
}

const { project } = Astro.props;
const { Content } = await project.render();
---
&lt;Layout title={project.data.title}&gt;
  &lt;div class="prose mx-auto px-4 py-10"&gt;
    &lt;h1&gt;{project.data.title}&lt;/h1&gt;
    &lt;p&gt;{project.data.description}&lt;/p&gt;
    &lt;hr /&gt;
    &lt;Content /&gt; &lt;!-- This renders your Markdown content --&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/Layout&gt;
</code></pre>
                </div>
                <p>Now, if you go to `/projects/astro-rebuild-guide` in your dev server, you will see a fully rendered page for your project!</p>
            </article>
        </main>
        <footer class="text-center py-8 mt-12 footer">
            <p class="text-sm subheader-text">Astro Rebuild Guide | Section 7</p>
        </footer>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
